t address the structural causes of unemployment and inequality. Many households remain dependent on grants without a pathway to sustainable livelihoods. 8. **Educational and skills deficits**: The apartheid-era Bantu Education system left generations with poor schooling. While progress has been made, many schools in poor areas still underperform, limiting upward mobility. In summary, apartheid created a deeply unequal and spatially divided society, and dismantling those structures requires sustained, inclusive economic growth, effective governance, and targeted social policies—which have been only partially achieved. Poverty has decreased in absolute terms since 1994, but relative poverty and extreme inequality remain stubbornly high.
